Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.70,0:00:05.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been dull without\Nso many orders lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.00,0:00:07.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've been too busy up to now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.00,0:00:10.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like it's been Black Friday.\NWe've been working too hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.03,0:00:11.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we took our case to\Nan animal rights group—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.80,0:00:16.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,or whatever the right outfit is, we might\Nbe able to get fair compensation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.62,0:00:21.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, you're really starting\Nto sound like a human, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.63,0:00:24.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We need to assert our rights, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.20,0:00:30.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These days, cats are creatures\Nthat deserve respect,\Nnot the property of human beings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.50,0:00:32.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the trend out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.78,0:00:38.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cats are cats. I think you're\Noverstating the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.00,0:00:42.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I do agree with you that\Ncats are deserving of some dignity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.70,0:00:45.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I wish they would\Ntake a page from us,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.20,0:00:50.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but unlike us furry beasts,\Nthose hairless, naked\Nanimals are heartless.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.15,0:00:53.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It may not do us any\Ngood to count on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.00,0:00:57.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Guys, supper's ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.90,0:01:15.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sitting under the {\i1}kotatsu {\i0}like this,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.76,0:01:18.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm kind of getting\Na craving for ice cream.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.02,0:01:24.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! Grandma, you meanie!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.31,0:01:26.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want ice cream!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.01,0:01:27.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't have any.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.07,0:01:29.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wah! I hate you!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.32,0:01:42.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ordinarily, right now,\Nthere'd be some boring news on the TV,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.08,0:01:45.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and Mom would be putting\Nher gross cooking on the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.80,0:01:49.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Her mom hated us\Nsomething terrible, didn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.70,0:01:54.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was someone who\Ncouldn't even tell the difference\Nbetween cat hair and ordinary dust.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.43,0:01:57.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wish I could go back home.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.90,0:02:05.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There she goes, wishing\Nfor the impossible again.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.69,0:02:08.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For heaven's sake,\Nshe doesn't understand a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.36,0:02:11.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you think so?\NMizuho is 16 years old now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.50,0:02:14.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If she were a cat, it would be crazy\Nif she hadn't had any kittens yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.60,0:02:19.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, aren't you a modern cat?\NThose animal groups would\Nhave something to say about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.70,0:02:20.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, buzz off.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.03,0:02:25.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mizuho is still a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.15,0:02:36.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She couldn't survive without us around.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.00,0:02:40.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's have some ice cream.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.18,0:02:44.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll give you this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.73,0:02:47.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! Not until you get back.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.50,0:02:52.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did she want us to bring this time?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.53,0:02:54.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ice cream.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.35,0:02:55.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By when?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.35,0:02:56.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She said right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.95,0:02:58.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is there time?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.17,0:03:00.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm... we'll try our best.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.33,0:03:15.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You there! Are you here as warriors?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.13,0:03:17.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, we're...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.60,0:03:19.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then why are you here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.40,0:03:22.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're... You see, we just want...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.50,0:03:25.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We want you to make up with Seiji.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.35,0:03:28.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your little quarrel is\Nbothering everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.16,0:03:33.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In this world,\Nthere is only the duel\Nbetween me and my brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.41,0:03:35.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whew, we made it in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.31,0:03:39.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you don't want to get\Ncaught in the middle of it,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.12,0:03:41.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then leave this world!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.19,0:03:45.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whoa, scary.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.85,0:03:47.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, what do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.38,0:03:52.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you this is what would happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.05,0:03:58.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your twin brother is quite, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.13,0:04:00.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...grouchy, isn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.31,0:04:01.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.35,0:04:04.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Unlike me, he's really narrow minded.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.40,0:04:08.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, is it true that the cause of your\Nfighting is a single strand of hair?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.30,0:04:09.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.30,0:04:13.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have 110,635 hairs,\Nwhile Sou has 110,634!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.69,0:04:16.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have one more hair than he does.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.40,0:04:18.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've counted a million times,\Nso there's no mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.33,0:04:21.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Talk about wigging out over nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.07,0:04:24.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Heh, I think so, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.71,0:04:27.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he would just be honest about me\Nbeating him, this would all be over.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.86,0:04:30.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, Nagara and Mizuho,\Nthanks for coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.54,0:04:33.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was right to talk to Nozomi about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.75,0:04:35.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll do whatever we can.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.30,0:04:36.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.84,0:04:40.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We got caught up in this\Nand didn't know what to do.\NMs. Aki has gone off\Nsomewhere else, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.04,0:04:45.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.20,0:04:46.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that look for?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.31,0:04:49.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing. I was just wondering how\Nlong you were going to keep that up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.70,0:04:51.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, cram it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.07,0:05:00.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How mature is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.99,0:05:01.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.37,0:05:12.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gah! Repulsive bunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.88,0:05:14.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Every last one of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.70,0:05:16.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Poor fellow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.35,0:05:19.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He goes off in a huff\Nand sulks when he feels snubbed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.30,0:05:22.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll wager he got shot down by Nozomi.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.10,0:05:24.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He can't win her heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.40,0:05:25.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Harsh, but accurate.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.97,0:05:30.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we're going to change the world,\Nwe need the power those twins have.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.32,0:05:32.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.19,0:05:34.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...we only need one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.44,0:05:37.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dosukoi!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.44,0:05:39.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrong! Watch me do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.97,0:05:43.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dosukoi!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.43,0:05:46.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Private Kaga, you try it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.98,0:05:50.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dosukoi!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.59,0:05:59.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you! This is a\Ndamn fine piece of meat!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.84,0:06:01.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where did you get it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.75,0:06:04.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-It was given to me by Seiji!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.60,0:06:05.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Gottsuan!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.90,0:06:08.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you "{\i1}gottsuan{\i0}" me, you moron!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.64,0:06:11.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought I told you not\Nto get too close to him!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.35,0:06:12.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Gottsuan{\i0}—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.40,0:06:12.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.40,0:06:15.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...can't you keep your promises?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.32,0:06:16.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.32,0:06:21.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those two twins really are fighting each\Nother over a single strand of hair, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.95,0:06:24.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, that's what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.10,0:06:25.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait, you're not thinking...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.80,0:06:27.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. That's what I'm thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.95,0:06:31.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We pluck a hair off the one who has more,\Nand show it to both of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.00,0:06:33.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you think it will really be that easy?\NMm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.69,0:06:36.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can you think of a better way?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.79,0:06:39.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm... How about a hair transplant?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.17,0:06:44.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It seemed like there was a power\Nholdover for this sort of thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.18,0:06:58.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,W-Was that...?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.40,0:07:00.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, "Reverse."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.01,0:07:10.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How should we compete this time around?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.85,0:07:15.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Reverse," the power the twins possess,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.00,0:07:18.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is able to rewind everything,\Nand reset the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.30,0:07:26.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was suggested that if that happened,\Nthen those of us in stasis
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.75,0:07:26.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,could possibly return to\Njust before we went adrift.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.95,0:07:28.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was suggested?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.45,0:07:31.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the bottom of a giant crater.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.30,0:07:34.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This place could have been reset\Nany number of times already.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.64,0:07:38.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But, since it's a reset,\Nthe twins don't seem to remember it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.45,0:07:40.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess they wouldn't, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.48,0:07:44.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Moreover, since both\Ntwins can use "Reverse,"
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.45,0:07:46.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,even if one of them uses "Reverse,"
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.45,0:07:51.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if the other one uses "Reverse" too,\Nthen that rewinding gets\Nrewound back to the way it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.05,0:07:55.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And that's how these two twins' conflict\Nhas gone on for thousands of years.\NThey call it a "Reverse-Reverse."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.42,0:08:00.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but it's not just Sou and Seiji\Nworking their powers.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.95,0:08:04.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's also the duel that's always being\Ncarried on when their power activates.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.62,0:08:06.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Duel?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.15,0:08:08.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.00,0:08:44.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, that's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.04,0:08:47.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So there are cheat-code powers\Nthat let you do resets, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.34,0:08:49.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.10,0:08:49.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.01,0:08:55.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}"Sou Seiji"...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.19,0:09:00.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? You mean those two\Naren't twins after all?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.40,0:09:01.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does this mean...?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.50,0:09:07.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you feel pathetic?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.50,0:09:09.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You keep losing to yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.60,0:09:12.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That guy isn't me! {\i1}I'm {\i0}me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.06,0:09:14.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you like some help?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.06,0:09:15.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.93,0:09:18.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You may have started out being the same,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.41,0:09:20.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but you're different now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.63,0:09:24.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll beat him on my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.45,0:09:27.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're a believer, too, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.16,0:09:34.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is God's divine protection.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.48,0:09:42.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They look like they're the same,\Nbut they aren't perfectly similar.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.41,0:09:44.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are slight variations in each copy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.50,0:09:46.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Keep it to yourself, dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.80,0:09:47.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.16,0:09:52.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you been listening in the whole time?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.10,0:09:54.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, starting at some point.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.53,0:09:58.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It speaks pretty poorly of your\Ncharacter not to say anything until now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.35,0:10:00.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I could never find the\Nright moment to mention it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.64,0:10:06.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nyamazon stuff is essentially\Na bunch of copies, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.65,0:10:08.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why ask me?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.38,0:10:09.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.70,0:10:12.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because you're the\None doing the copying, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.38,0:10:16.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know what? I can appreciate you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.55,0:10:19.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're unusually negative for a dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.40,0:10:22.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But more than anything,\Nyou're good to Mizuho.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.55,0:10:25.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason we kept it to\Nourselves is for Mizuho's sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.71,0:10:30.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If this got out, she's the one\Nthe blame would fall on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.45,0:10:36.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then again, if this had gotten out,\Nthey would have been able to go home\Nfor certain when they had the chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.70,0:10:39.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Back to the future they wanted.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.46,0:10:43.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure you kept it\Nto yourselves for {\i1}her {\i0}sake?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.52,0:10:45.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you insinuating?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.30,0:10:49.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That you're actually doing it\Nfor yourselves, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.35,0:10:50.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're afraid that if you leave Mizuho—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.99,0:10:51.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.56,0:10:55.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That girl\Ncan't get by without me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.72,0:10:59.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't think that's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.32,0:11:08.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The first one who noticed was that boy\Nwho is unusually smart for a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.82,0:11:12.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...fifty USB cables,\Nand a box of Sudakosan Taro.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.80,0:11:20.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A crowd-funded game I once\Nwrote for the PocketGame.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.15,0:11:21.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You {\i0}wrote? Badass.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.74,0:11:25.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm. What's more,\Nonly one was ever sold.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.00,0:11:29.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It became known as a legendary\None-of-a-kind game among the fans.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.63,0:11:32.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah? You Indians are something else.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.73,0:11:33.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an}So what kind of game is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.38,0:11:36.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}It's a highly-insidious,\Nimpossibly-hard game.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.45,0:11:40.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}The goal is to encounter\Na single predetermined tick
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.45,0:11:44.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}out of trillions of possible classmates,\Nand have it declare its love for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.70,0:11:44.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}It's a romantic simulation game.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.90,0:11:47.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whoa, that sounds super-fun!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.44,0:11:50.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I worked extra-hard on\Nworking out the ticks' emotions.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.61,0:11:55.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyhow, I need it to refer to for\Nthis next world we're conquering.\NIs that okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.35,0:11:56.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.69,0:11:57.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, but these are off-limits.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.40,0:12:03.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've made a few orders of my own,\Nbut those cats won't bring\Nme anything that's alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.70,0:12:05.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aw, I was afraid of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.50,0:12:07.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you for your business.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.68,0:12:29.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The only one of its kind in\Nthe world, and now there's...\N...two of them...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.19,0:12:35.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have been copied.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.15,0:12:44.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He knew that he did not fully\Nunderstand both his and Mizuho's powers.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.66,0:12:47.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what do you think I should do?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.70,0:12:50.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is my power, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.58,0:12:56.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was then that he chose a\Ndifferent subject to investigate.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.92,0:12:59.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you all copies, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.99,0:13:05.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's likely that the nature of\N"Nyamazon," Mizuho's power, is copying.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.05,0:13:06.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if that's the case...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.56,0:13:09.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those cats can't bring living creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.81,0:13:11.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It doesn't add up.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.92,0:13:17.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was definitely close to\Nthe truth about going adrift.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.32,0:13:19.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mizuho, can I borrow your cat?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.32,0:13:21.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's something I want to investigate.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.45,0:13:23.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.40,0:13:24.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, hey...!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.83,0:13:27.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.46,0:13:34.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are a cat. Your name is Tora.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.71,0:13:39.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you the one who coughed up a\Nhairball on my keyboard two days ago?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.67,0:13:44.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good. Okay, next question.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.15,0:13:47.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This one has to do...\N...with how you typically\Nbring us the things you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.55,0:13:52.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The things you bring back with you...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.69,0:13:54.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...are copies from the world\Nwe're from, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.48,0:13:57.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you answer me, I'll give you this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.51,0:14:02.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good boy. Next question.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.86,0:14:05.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys are lying to us, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.12,0:14:08.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You really can bring back\Nliving creatures, can't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.12,0:14:13.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've been keeping that from us.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.55,0:14:17.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because if people found out, it would\Nput Mizuho in a precarious spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.70,0:14:23.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it, then. The reason we went\Nadrift is because Mizuho's power—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.14,0:14:26.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wah! Hey, what are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.15,0:14:27.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.12,0:14:36.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was terrified that he\Nwould announce it to everyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.79,0:14:40.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(770,0)}but instead, he went off on his\Nsolo journey without saying a word.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.00,0:14:43.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has a fine character,\Nfor being so hairless.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.36,0:14:49.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, it's not as though Mizuho\Nwas the only cause of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.45,0:14:49.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Going adrift was nothing that could be\Nstopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.78,0:14:52.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was well aware of that fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.77,0:14:58.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When we gave him those sea monkeys\Nas a going-away present,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.00,0:14:59.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he seemed to be quite delighted.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.39,0:15:11.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wish I could go back home.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.03,0:15:13.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How is it possible...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.10,0:15:17.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...that things have changed so much\Nover a single strand of hair?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.13,0:15:25.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not a very tasty-looking animal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.41,0:15:30.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then again,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.41,0:15:32.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is it even possible that two copies were\Nmade of someone from our own world?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.41,0:15:36.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That kind of sounds like\Nsomeone screwed up their order, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.00,0:15:39.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could it be that two copies just\Nhappened to be made by accident?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.45,0:15:47.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once they bring Kaga back,\Nwe'll have all of us together.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.30,0:15:50.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once we are, I wonder if we could\Nget you to take us to another world.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.78,0:15:51.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.80,0:15:55.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We aren't leaving here\Nuntil Ms. Aki returns.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.36,0:15:57.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.60,0:16:01.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go thinking that there's a place\Nfor people like you anywhere you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.95,0:16:11.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me, when you say a "place,"\Nare you talking about this child's room
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.11,0:16:11.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that you recreated from your own home?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.49,0:16:15.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you don't have a power,\Nyou can't live on your own, can you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.33,0:16:18.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone has to be there to help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.16,0:16:22.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right. I may have been able\Nto survive in this world thanks to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.00,0:16:25.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then do as I tell you to.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.89,0:16:31.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then again, even so,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.00,0:16:31.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll thank you to let me\Npick my place for myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.40,0:16:34.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't do anything by yourself, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.60,0:16:36.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Admit it already.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.40,0:16:39.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're excess\Nbaggage for everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.39,0:16:41.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just because you have your lofty opinions
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.35,0:16:43.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,doesn't mean you can change anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.45,0:16:49.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nozomi!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.53,0:16:51.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Leave her to herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.72,0:16:54.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's just going to keep\Nslowing everyone else down.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.03,0:16:57.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you really mean that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.20,0:16:58.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It would be...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.99,0:17:01.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...better if she didn't go with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.01,0:17:04.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not something that\Nyou get to decide, Asakaze.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.65,0:17:06.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's something for Nozomi to decide.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.94,0:17:14.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stay away from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.64,0:17:17.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not very good company right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.32,0:17:22.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering if someone would\Nput an end to all of this for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.52,0:17:28.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The truth is, those kinds of slippery\Nthoughts are all I've been thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.01,0:17:46.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I recognize this bear. It's the kind\Nthey give you to celebrate a birth.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.75,0:17:48.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had one at my place, too,\Nbut I threw it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.40,0:17:51.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why do you suppose that was?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.92,0:17:54.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because the cats came to live with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.15,0:17:57.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cats are nice and warm,\Nbut bears are cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.39,0:17:58.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,'Cause they're dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.39,0:18:03.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can talk to them,\Nbut they never respond,\Nand the consistency of their fur is\Ndifferent.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.75,0:18:05.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know, 'cause they're dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.14,0:18:07.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, well, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.16,0:18:09.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,threw mine away, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.54,0:18:22.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When night comes, she can't\Neven go up the stairs by herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.50,0:18:26.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll bet that right now,\Nshe's trembling in fear from the storm.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.69,0:18:33.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't live with her\Nin that house anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.67,0:18:37.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know that we're going\Nto end up getting split up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.30,0:18:43.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's just a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.65,0:18:46.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's still just a little—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.58,0:19:00.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've always wondered...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.90,0:19:03.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...what is the point of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.07,0:19:07.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What can you do with that toy?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.89,0:19:11.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just how far have you fallen?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.09,0:19:15.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ever since that day, when another me\Nstarted walking around on his own,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.07,0:19:18.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it has been my only wish\Nto do away with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.00,0:19:20.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's more than you can handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.45,0:19:23.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You and I both have the same power.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.31,0:19:28.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You do actually understand, don't you?\NThat Seiji can't win?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.11,0:19:30.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why you pray.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.57,0:19:32.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.15,0:19:37.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catch!\NToday, we fight with these!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.53,0:19:40.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.00,0:19:43.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Always reaching the\Nsame outcome must be dull, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.08,0:20:05.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These are special guns.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.44,0:20:13.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is what's called a "Skip."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.88,0:20:21.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At last, my wish has come true.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.15,0:20:28.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sakura!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.78,0:20:35.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop! That's my sacrifice to God!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.80,0:20:43.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This cat is still alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.57,0:20:47.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing ever changes if you\Nkeep clinging to somebody!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.31,0:20:51.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You just have to deal\Nwith things yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.33,0:21:07.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's too cold out here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.50,0:21:19.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I did manage to change, thanks to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.63,0:21:25.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because you showed me the light.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.50,0:21:34.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.87,0:21:35.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.90,0:21:39.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.40,0:21:41.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You win.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.07,0:21:44.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How does it feel,\Nnow that you're the victor?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.90,0:21:48.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, somehow...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.14,0:21:50.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...it feels awfully hollow.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.04,0:21:51.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.17,0:21:57.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because now, I don't know...\N...what I should do.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.52,0:22:05.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, they're back.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.35,0:22:11.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the medicine I ordered for Sakura.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.50,0:22:17.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm? Say, what is she\Nalways doing, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.30,0:22:20.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sakura is a born lazybones.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.60,0:22:24.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm, she seems like the smartest one, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.14,0:22:27.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have to get going.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.90,0:22:31.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What fun is it to go\Ntogether with those guys?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.30,0:22:35.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, you may be right, but still...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.13,0:22:38.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.98,0:22:41.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nozomi, I'll be in touch.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.95,0:22:42.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.55,0:22:44.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bye-bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.07,0:22:58.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All that remains is a gaping hole, huh?
